<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Bernhard of Saxe-Weimar</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1604">1604</a>–<a href="/years/1639">1639</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a> · Also known as Bernard of Saxe-Weimar · Of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/house-of-wettin">House of Wettin</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Bernhard of Saxe-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/weimar">Weimar</a> was a German prince and one of the leading Protestant generals of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/thirty-years-war">Thirty Years' War</a>. Serving <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sweden">Sweden</a>, he took command at the Battle of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-lutzen-1632">Lützen</a> in 1632 after <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gustavus-adolphus">Gustavus Adolphus</a> was killed, but was heavily defeated at Nördlingen in 1634. He then fought for <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a>, captured the fortress of Breisach in 1638 and hoped to rule <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alsace">Alsace</a>, but died suddenly in 1639.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/bernhard-of-saxe-weimar.jpg" alt="Bernhard of Saxe-Weimar" width="320" height="469" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Rijksmuseum · CC0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Portret_van_Bernhard,_hertog_van_Saksen-Weimar_Theatrum_pontificum,_imperatorum,_regum,_ducum_(serietitel),_RP-P-1911-5117.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>Near the village of Wittenweiher, now part of Schwanau in Baden-Württemberg, an army under the Protestant general <b>Bernhard of Saxe-Weimar</b> defeated imperial troops in the Thirty Years' War.</blockquote><a href="/today-in-history/august-9">9 August in history</a></li><li><blockquote>In the Thirty Years' War, imperial and Spanish forces under the future Emperor Ferdinand III and the Cardinal-Infante Ferdinand crushed the Swedes and their German allies under Gustav Horn and <b>Bernhard of Saxe-Weimar</b>.</blockquote><a href="/today-in-history/september-6">6 September in history</a></li><li><blockquote>The duchy was repeatedly divided among brothers, and in 1640 the Duchy of Saxe-Gotha split off, while <b>Bernhard of Saxe-Weimar</b> became a famous Protestant general in the Thirty Years' War.</blockquote><a href="/state/duchy-of-saxe-weimar">Duchy of Saxe-Weimar</a></li></ul></section>
